IMPORT prelude

-- Resource Sustainability Act 2019 (Singapore) -- what the Act asks of shops and shoppers: free take-back of old electrical and
-- electronic goods on delivery (s 14) and in large stores (s 15); the disposable carrier bag charge, with registration and
-- deregistration of retailers (ss 23A to 23H); the beverage container deposit and its refund (ss 23Q, 23U, 23X); the maximum
-- penalties for those offences and the composition cap (s 49).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December 2021), informal
-- consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/RSA2019.txt (SSO "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026"). The latest
-- amendments annotated are by Act 14 of 2023 (wef 26/05/2023, 08/03/2024 and 12/07/2024) and S 582/2024 (the Schedule, wef
-- 12/07/2024).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0066 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has yet asked a sharper
-- question. SCOPED to the provisions a shopper or a shop meets. Not encoded: producer registration and the licensed-scheme
-- obligations of e-waste producers (ss 8 to 13, 16, 17); packaging reports and 3R plans (Part 4); bag-charge reports, records and
-- publication (ss 23I to 23L); producers' and return-point operators' duties under the beverage scheme beyond the refund (ss 23O,
-- 23P, 23R to 23T, 23V, 23W); food waste (Part 5); scheme licensing (Part 6); enforcement powers and appeals (Parts 7, 8).
-- Everything the Act leaves to be "prescribed" -- which products are regulated, which retailers are regulated, the turnover
-- threshold, the deposit amount, exempt bags -- is a parameter or a flag here: no subsidiary legislation was read.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the example rows (the writing-l4-rules skill was not
-- available in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Resource Sustainability Act 2019 -- shops and shoppers`

§§ `14 -- take-back on delivery`

-- s 14(1): where a retailer supplies a regulated consumer product to a consumer and "delivers, or causes the delivery of, the
-- supplied product to any premises specified by the consumer", the consumer may require the retailer to collect and dispose of
-- "another regulated consumer product ... that is of the same class or type as the supplied product".
-- s 2(1): "consumer" means "an individual who purchases or intends to purchase ... for household use or private consumption".
-- s 14(2): the retailer (a) must collect at the time of delivery or another agreed time, and (b) "must not demand or require the
-- person to pay any consideration for the collection and disposal ... (such as the cost of any labour or transport)".
-- s 14(3): "without reasonable excuse" -- fine up to $5,000.
GIVEN `the buyer is a consumer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the supplied product is a regulated consumer product` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the retailer delivered it to premises the consumer specified` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the unwanted product is of the same class or type` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the consumer requires collection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the retailer must collect the unwanted product free` IF
        `the buyer is a consumer`
    AND `the supplied product is a regulated consumer product`
    AND `the retailer delivered it to premises the consumer specified`
    AND `the unwanted product is of the same class or type`
    AND `the consumer requires collection`

GIVEN `the duty arose` IS A BOOLEAN, `the retailer collected` IS A BOOLEAN, `the retailer demanded payment` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the retailer had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the retailer commits the s 14(3) offence` IF
        `the duty arose`
    AND ((NOT `the retailer collected`) OR `the retailer demanded payment`)
    AND (NOT `the retailer had a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `15 -- in-store take-back at large retailers`

-- s 15(1): applies only to "designated regulated consumer products" and to a retailer who owns or occupies premises "with a floor
-- area of or more than 300 sqm (or such other area prescribed in substitution)" from which a designated product is supplied.
-- s 15(2): where a designated product "is brought to a retailer's premises for disposal" and is of the same class or type as that
-- supplied at those premises, "the retailer must accept" it. Nothing in s 15 requires the person to buy anything.
-- s 15(3): "without reasonable excuse" -- fine up to $5,000.
GIVEN `the product is a designated regulated consumer product` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the floor area in square metres` IS A NUMBER,
      `the same class or type is supplied at those premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the retailer must accept the product in store` IF
        `the product is a designated regulated consumer product`
    AND `the floor area in square metres` AT LEAST 300
    AND `the same class or type is supplied at those premises`

§§ `23A -- disposable carrier bags`

-- s 23A: "disposable carrier bag" means packaging "in the form of a bag with handles (other than a reusable bag)" provided by a
-- retailer to pack goods purchased by a customer, "whether or not the bag is in fact so used by the customer".
-- "reusable bag" means any bag with handles that (a) is made primarily of washable woven fabric; (b) is made primarily of plastic or
-- synthetic polymers "of a prescribed minimum thickness or density"; (c) "has the ability to hold a prescribed minimum weight"; or
-- (d) is prescribed as reusable. The definition names no material for a disposable bag: a paper bag with handles that meets none of
-- (a) to (d) is a disposable carrier bag.
DECLARE Bag
    HAS `has handles` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is made primarily of washable woven fabric` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is plastic of the prescribed minimum thickness or density` IS A BOOLEAN
        `can hold the prescribed minimum weight` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is prescribed as reusable` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the bag` IS A Bag
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bag is reusable` IF
        `the bag`'s `has handles`
    AND (   `the bag`'s `is made primarily of washable woven fabric`
         OR `the bag`'s `is plastic of the prescribed minimum thickness or density`
         OR `the bag`'s `can hold the prescribed minimum weight`
         OR `the bag`'s `is prescribed as reusable`)

GIVEN `the bag` IS A Bag
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bag is a disposable carrier bag` IF
    `the bag`'s `has handles` AND (NOT `the bag is reusable` `the bag`)

§§ `23F, 23G, 23H -- the charge`

-- s 23F(1): "a registered retailer must impose and collect a charge of an amount no less than the prescribed amount for each
-- disposable carrier bag that the registered retailer provides to a customer who purchases any goods". (2): not for prescribed bags,
-- prescribed persons, prescribed circumstances or prescribed retailers. s 23A: "prescribed amount" means "$0.05 or another amount
-- prescribed in substitution". The charge is a floor: a retailer may charge more (s 23J(1)(a) speaks of "any amount collected in excess
-- of the prescribed amount").
-- s 23G: the retailer "must not provide any reimbursement for a charge ... whether in money or in kind".
-- s 23H: the charge must be communicated as prescribed and, where a receipt is given, set out "as a separate item".
-- ss 23F(3), 23G(2), 23H(2): fine up to $10,000 or 3 months or both; each "is a strict liability offence".
GIVEN `the retailer is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `the bag` IS A Bag, `the customer purchases goods` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a prescribed exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a bag charge must be imposed` IF
        `the retailer is registered`
    AND `the bag is a disposable carrier bag` `the bag`
    AND `the customer purchases goods`
    AND (NOT `a prescribed exception applies`)

GIVEN `the charge in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the charge is enough` IF `the charge in dollars` AT LEAST 0.05

§§ `23B, 23C, 23D -- registration and deregistration`

-- s 23B(1): a regulated retailer whose "annual turnover for any trigger year ... exceeds the prescribed annual turnover" for its class
-- must, unless already registered for that class, apply to be registered. (2): fine up to $10,000 or 3 months or both; (4) strict
-- liability.
-- s 23C(1)(a)(ii): where the trigger year T is 2022 or later, the application must be made "before ... 30 June of year T + 1".
-- s 23C(3)(b): registration then begins on "1 January of year T + 2" and continues until deregistration. (For T = 2021 both dates
-- were prescribed; not encoded.)
-- s 23D(1): a registered retailer may apply to be deregistered if (a) it ceases to be a regulated retailer of that class, or (b) "the
-- annual turnover ... for each of 3 consecutive years does not exceed the prescribed annual turnover". (2): 30 days' notice of a
-- cessation.
GIVEN `is a regulated retailer` IS A BOOLEAN, `the turnover` IS A NUMBER, `the prescribed turnover` IS A NUMBER,
      `is already registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the retailer must apply to register` IF
        `is a regulated retailer`
    AND `the turnover` GREATER THAN `the prescribed turnover`
    AND (NOT `is already registered`)

GIVEN `the trigger year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year by whose 30 June the application must be made` MEANS `the trigger year` PLUS 1

GIVEN `the trigger year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year on whose 1 January registration begins` MEANS `the trigger year` PLUS 2

GIVEN `has ceased to be a regulated retailer of the class` IS A BOOLEAN, `turnover year 1` IS A NUMBER, `turnover year 2` IS A NUMBER,
      `turnover year 3` IS A NUMBER, `the prescribed turnover` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the retailer may apply to deregister` IF
        `has ceased to be a regulated retailer of the class`
    OR  (    `turnover year 1` AT MOST `the prescribed turnover`
         AND `turnover year 2` AT MOST `the prescribed turnover`
         AND `turnover year 3` AT MOST `the prescribed turnover`)

§§ `23Q -- the deposit on a beverage`

-- s 23Q(3): where X supplies a beverage product affixed with a deposit mark to Y, "X must collect from Y, and Y must give to X, the
-- amount of the deposit". (4): X may refuse to supply if Y refuses, "but X may waive Y's giving of the amount of the deposit".
-- (5): "X must not waive ... if X receives any consideration in money for the supply". (6): if X waives and Y later receives the
-- deposit from its own customer, Y must pass it to X within the prescribed period. (7): first conviction fine up to $5,000; second or
-- subsequent up to $10,000 or 3 months or both. (8): the deposit is not "any part of the price". The amount is prescribed (s 23Q(2)).
GIVEN `the seller receives money for the beverage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seller may waive the deposit` IF NOT `the seller receives money for the beverage`

GIVEN `the deposit was waived` IS A BOOLEAN, `the buyer received the deposit from its own customer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the buyer must still pay the deposit to the seller` IF
    `the deposit was waived` AND `the buyer received the deposit from its own customer`

§§ `23U -- the refund at a return point`

-- s 23U(1): if a person presents "an empty beverage container affixed with a deposit mark and barcode" at a return point, the operator
-- "must accept the beverage container and refund the deposit". (2) not (a) if the mark or barcode "is so damaged that it cannot be read
-- or scanned"; (b) outside operating hours specified at the return point; (c) if the operator "reasonably believes" no deposit was
-- provided to the scheme licensee or the deposit was previously refunded; (d) other prescribed circumstances.
-- s 23U(3): "without reasonable excuse" -- fine up to $10,000 or 3 months or both.
GIVEN `presented at a return point` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an empty container with a deposit mark and barcode` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the mark or barcode cannot be read or scanned` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `outside the operating hours specified at the return point` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the operator reasonably believes no deposit was paid or it was already refunded` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `another prescribed exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator must refund the deposit` IF
        `presented at a return point`
    AND `an empty container with a deposit mark and barcode`
    AND (NOT `the mark or barcode cannot be read or scanned`)
    AND (NOT `outside the operating hours specified at the return point`)
    AND (NOT `the operator reasonably believes no deposit was paid or it was already refunded`)
    AND (NOT `another prescribed exception applies`)

§§ `Penalties and s 49 composition`

-- The maximum on (first) conviction for each offence encoded, as the penalty subsection states it. s 14(4) and s 15(4): disposing of
-- collected e-waste other than through a person operating a licensed scheme -- fine up to $10,000, and the prosecution need not prove
-- knowledge (ss 14(5), 15(5)). s 23X: affixing a deposit mark to a container that is not a beverage container without a scheme
-- licensee's written authority -- "without reasonable excuse", $10,000 or 3 months or both.
-- s 49(1): an authorised officer may compound an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" by collecting a sum not exceeding
-- "the lower of" (a) "one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence" and (b) $5,000.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `s 14(3) not collecting, or charging for, take-back on delivery`
    `s 14(4) disposing of taken-back e-waste outside a licensed scheme`
    `s 15(3) refusing in-store take-back`
    `s 23B(2) not applying to register for the bag charge`
    `s 23F(3) not charging for a disposable carrier bag`
    `s 23G(2) reimbursing the bag charge`
    `s 23H(2) not showing the bag charge`
    `s 23Q(7) waiving the deposit on a sale for money`
    `s 23U(3) refusing a deposit refund`
    `s 23X(2) misusing the deposit mark`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine on first conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 14(3) not collecting, or charging for, take-back on delivery` THEN 5000
    WHEN `s 15(3) refusing in-store take-back` THEN 5000
    WHEN `s 23Q(7) waiving the deposit on a sale for money` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months on first conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 14(3) not collecting, or charging for, take-back on delivery` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 14(4) disposing of taken-back e-waste outside a licensed scheme` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 15(3) refusing in-store take-back` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 23Q(7) waiving the deposit on a sale for money` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 3

-- Which offences the text words "without reasonable excuse", and which it declares "a strict liability offence". s 14(4) and s 23Q(7)
-- are neither (s 14(5) only dispenses with proof of knowledge of three facts).
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is worded without reasonable excuse` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 14(3) not collecting, or charging for, take-back on delivery` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 15(3) refusing in-store take-back` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 23U(3) refusing a deposit refund` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 23X(2) misusing the deposit mark` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is declared strict liability` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 23B(2) not applying to register for the bag charge` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 23F(3) not charging for a disposable carrier bag` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 23G(2) reimbursing the bag charge` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 23H(2) not showing the bag charge` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most a composition may collect` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`the maximum fine on first conviction` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000
